    "media:imagetext": "Flying the West better than anyone\nWith our \"hub\" operation through Salt Lake City, Wester\nas with other frequent fiyer programs. And theres no rec-\nhas more flights to more cities in the West than any other\nords to keep, no coupons to turn in. Our computer keeps a\nairline. With one of the Nation's most modern and spacious\ncomplete record of your travel mileage.\ninternational airports, Salt Lake City offers superior pas-\nsenger facilities.\nBecause of our hub, Wester can take you to every\nmajor city and resort area in the West. Wester offers more\nnonstops and more first flights out every morning to more\ncities in the West than any other airline. In all, Western\nAirlines serves more than 60 cities in the U.S., Canada and\nMexico.\nHorizon Club Hospitality\nOn the ground, you'll feel right at home at our private\nHorizon Club airport lounges. Club members will find the\nwarm hospitality of our lounges in 13 major airports\nA Cargo Airline, Too\nAt Western, we don't just fly passengers, were cargo ex-\nperts, too. Our Speed Pak service moves small packages\nup to 70# between any two Western Airlines airports in the\nU.S. including Alaska and Hawaii for just $40. Our Mini-Pak\nprovides the same service for letters and reports for only\n$20. For your larger cargo needs, you can reserve space\non a specific flight with our Priority Reserved Freight pro-\ngram. Door-to-Door freight service plus a new shipper\nowned \"C\" container have been added to our family of\nefficient cargo services.\nthroughout our system.\nTravel Pass II\nWestern pioneered the concept of frequent flyer benefits in\n1980. Today we offer the simplest, fastest and most re-\nwarding frequent flyer program in the sky-Travel Pass !.\nEar free trips and first class upgrades almost twice as fast\nMore nonstops from more Western cities. Low Country\nfares. Horizon Club hospitality and Travel Pass I!. A full line\nof cargo services.\nEvery day we live up to our name by flying the West\nbetter than anyone. What else would you expect from an\nairline named Wester.\nTA407 PRINTED IN USA\nWestern Airlines\nWeve got a name to live up to.\n102\n00..",
